From c50b284e69409efae35a5dd2a4114335378b6cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:59:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: say which levels Table 7 of CCM 001 defines

The comment of dvbridge_dv_level_known() said that the levels it knows (1
to 6, 8 to 11, 254 and 255) are those that a display uses by ETSI GS CCM
001, Table 7. Table 7 defines levels 1, 2 and 5 and has 0, 3, 4 and 6 to
255 reserved; the others are those that Dolby Vision RPUs carry as FFmpeg
reads them. The comment now says so, and quotes the rule that makes the
serializer leave other levels out. A comment only: nothing compiled
changes.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_metadata.h | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_metadata.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_metadata.h
index 9cbbcce..cb81049 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_metadata.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_metadata.h
@@ -267,8 +267,13 @@ static inline void dvbridge_dv_restart(struct dvbridge_dv *d)
     d->no_trims = no_trims;
     d->restart = true;
 }
-/* Hades: the extension levels that a display uses (CCM 001, Table 7). The others are reserved:
- * a display ignores them, and so does the serializer (instead of refusing the frame). */
+/* Hades: the extension levels that the serializer knows. ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1 defines 1, 2 and 5
+ * (Table 7: 0, 3, 4 and 6 to 255 are reserved there); the others here are those that Dolby Vision
+ * RPUs carry as FFmpeg reads them (dovi_rpudec.c): 4 and 6 of content mapping v2.9, 3, 8 to 11 and
+ * 254 of v4.0, and 255 (encoder data). A block of any other level is left out: CCM 001 has a
+ * display ignore a reserved level ("Blocks using values of ext_block_level that are reserved shall
+ * be ignored"), and the serializer does the same instead of refusing the frame. (It said that
+ * Table 7 named all of these.) */
 static inline bool dvbridge_dv_level_known(unsigned level)
 {
     return (level >= 1 && level <= 6) || (level >= 8 && level <= 11) || level == 254 || level == 255;
-- 
